| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **1**  | **VGG16 + VGG19 + ResNet101V2 + InceptionV3 + Ensemble Voting + LIME**   | PlantVillage; **54,305 images**, 38 disease classes | Combines four DL models to improve disease prediction and uses LIME to explain predictions                | Ensemble achieved **>93% overall accuracy**; soft voting performed best                               | Uses controlled PlantVillage images; no severity estimation, agrochemical recommendation or PQC | **Direct base paper for disease detection + XAI**                                 |
| **2**  | **Vision Transformer (ViT)**; systematic parameter optimization          | PlantVillage + additional databases                 | Studies patch size, resolution, embedding dimension, transformer depth, attention heads and MLP dimension | Reports **99.77% accuracy on PlantVillage** with optimized configuration                              | High performance on benchmark datasets doesn't automatically guarantee field robustness         | Supports your choice of **Transformer-based disease detection**                   |
| **3**  | **DETR + Swin Transformer + SAM2-UNet**                                  | Agricultural plant images under varied conditions   | Unified **classification + detection + segmentation + severity estimation**                               | Demonstrates an integrated disease diagnosis/severity pipeline                                        | More computationally demanding; difficult for a small capstone to reproduce completely          | Excellent reference for your **severity-estimation module**                       |
| **4**  | **CNN + Vision Transformer hybrid architecture**                         | Crop/leaf images in different environments          | Combines local CNN features with Transformer global attention                                             | Designed to improve robustness across environmental variations                                        | Hybrid architecture increases complexity and computational requirements                         | Gives you a possible **future enhancement**                                       |
| **5**  | **Deep Learning + Explainable AI**                                       | Plant disease images                                | Improves disease classification while explaining model decisions                                          | Demonstrates importance of interpretability for plant-disease diagnosis                               | Explainability does not itself guarantee correct diagnosis                                      | Supports your use of **Grad-CAM/XAI**                                             |
| **6**  | **Computer Vision + DL + ML + AI review**                                | Multiple plant-disease datasets from literature     | Reviews existing plant disease detection/diagnosis approaches                                             | Identifies trends including DL, few-shot learning and CV                                              | Review paper; doesn't provide a new implementation                                              | Excellent source for your **Chapter 2 background and research gaps**              |
| **7**  | **Self-Supervised Learning**                                             | Plant disease image datasets                        | Reviews generative, predictive, contrastive and hybrid SSL methods                                        | Highlights SSL as a solution to limited labelled agricultural data                                    | SSL approaches still face scalability, domain-shift and deployment challenges                   | Supports your argument about **field-data scarcity**                              |
| **8**  | **CNN + geospatial data + weather + soil moisture + satellite NDVI/LST** | >50,000 images; 15 crops; 25 diseases               | Combines visual disease detection with environmental/geospatial information                               | Reports **96.8% accuracy**                                                                            | Requires additional environmental/geospatial infrastructure                                     | Possible **future extension: image + environment → disease risk**                 |
| **9**  | **Deep Learning + Disease Classification + Pesticide Recommendation**    | Plant disease images                                | Connects disease identification directly to pesticide recommendation                                      | Demonstrates integrated disease-to-treatment workflow                                                 | Recommendation may be relatively disease-centric rather than severity/context-aware             | **Direct base paper for your agrochemical recommendation module**                 |
| **10** | **Deep Learning + Crop Disease Prediction + Pesticide Recommendation**   | Crop disease data/images                            | Integrates disease prediction and pesticide recommendation                                                | Demonstrates feasibility of combining diagnosis and treatment recommendation                          | Doesn't provide your PQC-secured architecture                                                   | One of your **closest papers overall**                                            |
| **11** | **DenseNet + image processing + pesticide recommendation**               | Plant disease images                                | Automated disease identification followed by pesticide recommendation; verification by plant pathologists | Reports **>92% disease-identification accuracy**                                                      | Limited contextual/environmental reasoning; no PQC                                              | Supports **DenseNet baseline + cloud deployment concept**                         |
| **12** | **ML/AI comparative pesticide recommendation**                           | Agricultural/pesticide recommendation data          | Compares ML/AI approaches for pesticide recommendation                                                    | Shows ML/AI can support smarter pesticide selection                                                   | Recommendation quality depends heavily on input features and knowledge base                     | Supports your **recommendation-engine design**                                    |
| **13** | **ML + rule-based recommendation**                                       | Soil NPK, pH, environmental parameters              | Combines ML crop recommendation with rule-based fertilizer recommendation                                 | Reports high crop recommendation performance and rule-based fertilizer recommendations                | Focuses on fertilizer/crop selection rather than disease-specific treatment                     | Strong evidence for using a **knowledge/rule-based agrochemical engine**          |
| **14** | **Post-Quantum Cryptography + IoT performance analysis**                 | Resource-constrained IoT devices                    | Studies PQC performance and optimization for constrained devices                                          | Finds PQC feasible for reasonably lightweight IoT but highlights computational/communication overhead | Standardization and optimization remain challenges                                              | Provides the foundation for your **PQC communication layer**                      |
| **15** | **PQC + IoT + Deep Learning**                                            | IoT/AI environments                                 | Investigates integration of quantum-resistant cryptography with DL-enabled IoT                            | Shows feasibility of combining AI and PQ security                                                     | Not agriculture-specific; security overhead must be evaluated                                   | Provides the bridge between **AI + IoT + PQC**, matching your unique architecture |










